          "requirement_id": "FAB-ELEC-004",
          "system": "fabrication_handoff",
          "package_id": "battery_power_carrier_mount_rev_a",
          "title": "Battery stand power carrier Rev F standard-battery access",
          "current_status": "prototype_release_mockup_required",
          "release_position": "Compact steel chassis-bolted battery stand: 3 mm 340 x 265 top tray/deck around a standard N70/27-class 318 x 180 x 230 battery envelope with central top terminals, removable battery hold-down and lift-out path, widened 660 x 310 front/radiator-side access ladder, folded aluminium side-mounted cutoff/kill-switch base/guard, one known 4 mm formed chassis saddle/upright bridge, and 4 mm slotted body-side offset bars. The saddle drops over the chassis rail from above, has legs down both sides, and is through-bolted through both saddle legs/chassis at the one pickup location. The offset bars stretch from the saddle/upright bridge toward the body/wing-side battery pocket so the tray/access-ladder offset can be configured around a 190 mm target with 160-230 mm retained adjustment. Relay Rev D mounts outside the battery footprint on the outboard/access edge with about 80 mm relay-to-battery service gap, using a flat 360 x 245 x 3 mm aluminium base mounted vertically and directly flat to the main metal service sheet plus exact 300 x 197 insulating sheet and the existing covered relay box; no separate relay cable-boot, output-cluster, or loom-card fabrication is added above it. The red relay power pipe enters the relay top hole closest to the battery, and the relay output power bundle leaves the second top relay hole. MIDI Rev D hinged enclosure mounts on a separated shallow top-front shelf whose leading edge starts at the battery leading-edge datum, with fuse 4 cutoff-switched power input through the input/bus-side grommet, five output-side grommets, and the far-side output enlarged for two power cables. Folded cutoff/kill-switch base/guard sits beside the MIDI enclosure, not after the MIDI outputs, with a 210 x 150 mm flat pattern, 170 x 110 mm finished face, and 20 mm lips bent upward around the 100A breaker/terminal side. Central battery positive enters the far-side cutoff/kill-switch stud first; the near-side cutoff output splits into two protected branches, one to the red relay power pipe and one to the MIDI fuse 4 grommeted input, with an 80 mm cable gutter and five-output fanout clearance. Final drilling/welding remains gated by battery-installed cavity map, LHD mock-up, chassis saddle measurement, offset-bar setting, 100A breaker body dimensions and stud spacing, battery-to-cutoff and cutoff-output cable lug sweeps, battery lift-out, relay cover access, relay top-hole cable sweep, bonnet clearance, steering/radiator/fan/hose clearance, and battery terminal orientation.",
          "notes": "User update 2026-05-16 relay/battery carrier correction: use Relay Rev D in the battery stand power carrier with the flat aluminium base mounted vertically and directly flat to the main metal service sheet; keep the exact insulating sheet and existing covered relay box only. The red relay power pipe enters the relay top hole closest to the battery, and the relay output power bundle exits the second top relay hole. Remove the separate red/black relay cable-boot/output-cluster/loom-card fabrication. Keep MIDI Rev D hinged enclosure from midi5_enclosure_rev_d and slotted body-side offset bars so the battery stand power carrier can be adjusted on the chassis saddle. Keep the widened access ladder at 660 x 310, the 340 x 265 tray around a 318 x 180 x 230 standard battery envelope, battery removal after hold-down removal, relay outside the battery footprint on the outboard/access edge, kill switch beside the MIDI enclosure, central battery positive to the far-side cutoff stud first, near-side cutoff output to relay and MIDI fuse 4, 80 mm cable gutter, five grommeted MIDI outputs, and far-side enlarged double-cable output clearance. Chassis fixing is a formed saddle over both rail sides, through-bolted at the one pickup location, with configurable 160-230 mm body-side offset bars.",
